// PS5MM's frame interpolation engine: RIFE (ncnn + Vulkan), hung under the
// picture engine's port like the media routes.
//
// Why it lives under 8002 and not in a slot of its own: RIFE holds no model in
// memory between calls worth a slot -- its three nets are a few MB, and the
// whole job is "two pictures in, one picture out". Slots are for engines that
// keep a resident model.
//
//   GET  /media/v1/interp/info     -> model dir, loaded, jobs
//   POST /media/v1/interpolate     { frame0: b64 png, frame1: b64 png,
//                                    timestep?: 0.5 }
//                                  -> { png: b64, ms: n }
//
// The model is loaded on the first request: a request at boot would fight the
// LM for the pool, and most sessions never touch interpolation.

